        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "Implemented `/app/pipeline_parallel.py` with `train_step_pipeline_afab`:\n\n**Design:**\n- **Layer partitioning:** `n_layers` split roughly evenly across `world_size` stages (remainder distributed to earlier ranks); each stage runs `model.model.layers[start:end]`.\n- **AFAB forward:** For every microbatch in order — rank 0 embeds input IDs via `model.model.embed_tokens`; intermediate/last ranks receive hidden states `[mb, seq, hidden]` from the previous rank with `dist.P2POp(dist.irecv)` (moved to device/dtype, then `requires_grad_(True)` so autograd tracks the boundary). Each stage runs its layers, and non-last stages send activations onward with a detached copy (autograd-connected tensor is kept locally).\n- **Loss:** On the last rank, applies `model.model.norm` + `model.lm_head`, computes cross-entropy against targets divided by the number of microbatches.\n- **AFAB backward:** After all forwards, backward passes run for all microbatches in order — last rank calls `.backward()` on its loss; other stages receive the output gradient from the next rank via P2P and call `out.backward(gradient=g)`, which propagates through local layers into parameters and the received-input leaf for further upstream propagation. Losses are summed and returned.\n- **world_size == 1** uses a straightforward local microbatch loop.\n\nNote: this container has no Python interpreter installed, so I couldn't execute tests here — but the file is syntactically clean and follows exactly the required communication pattern (no hooks used).",
            "session_id": "tb-7cf0a39942"
        }
